  "original_author_id": 0,
  "body": "From a quick glance, the following happens:\r\n- first GET request without any Authorization\r\n- first 401 response with `www-authenticate: Basic realm=`\r\n- second request with an `Authorization: Basic <redacted>` header\r\n  - the successful attempt receives a 200\r\n  - the failed attempt receives a 401 and not `www-authenticate` header\r\n  - the failed attempts makes again an authenticated request, which receives a 401 as well\r\n\r\n@SinTan1729 did you compare the 3 `Authorization: Basic ...` values?\r\n- the successful\r\n- the first failure\r\n- the second failure\r\n(they are base64 encoded - after decoding they should look like `OAUTH_USER:token`)\r\n\r\nAre they all different?\r\n\r\nApparently you didn't set `GIT_TRACE` (I can't see any `git-credential get` log line).",
